      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Visualize the air as two streams rushing past the wing: the faster stream over the top and the slower stream underneath. Due to the faster speed on top, the air molecules exert less force (lower pressure) on the curved upper surface. At the bottom, the air is moving slower, keeping the pressure higher, while the downward redirection of the entire airflow path provides the reactive upward force predicted by Newton's Third Law. A good mnemonic is: **Bernoulli explains the *pressure difference*; Newton explains the *reaction* to the deflecting air.**",
      "source": "target",
